<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato says 1996 budget deficit on track.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato says 1996 budget deficit on track.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said the government would meet its target for the budget deficit in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;The 1996 budget deficit figures are fine,&quot; Rato told a breakfast radio programme. &quot;The government is going to meet the targets it has set.&quot;</p>
<p>The government aims to reduce the budget deficit to 4.4 percent of GDP in 1996 from an estimated 5.8 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2161</p>
